      "title": "Tone Production",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** singing | **Difficulty:** 2/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Tone colour — bright, dark, breathy, focused — comes from vocal tract shaping, breath pressure, and resonance balance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "resonance",
      "title": "Resonance",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Chest resonance (lower notes), head resonance (higher). Mixed voice blends both. Forward placement ('mask' resonance) aids projection without pushing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vowel-uniformity",
      "title": "Vowel uniformity",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Keep vowel shape consistent across pitch changes. 'Ah' widening at high notes spreads tone thin."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "folk-context",
      "title": "Folk context",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Sean-nós embraces natural voice colour — not operatic uniformity. Match tone to song: lullaby vs drinking song vs lament."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "avoid",
      "title": "Avoid",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Pushing throat, excessive jaw tension, manufactured vibrato before basic pitch is stable."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
